    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2ab423e5-5c33-55b6-b24a-f57eede176fa",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the natural numbers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each set contains all the natural numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}$ contains the positive integers (natural numbers). By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{N}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}^{+}$ contains the positive real numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{R}^{+}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative real numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative rational numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{N}$, $\\mathbb{R}^{+}$, $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$, $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$ only.",
