      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets does the number $\\sqrt{0}$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we note that $\\sqrt{0}=0$ is zero.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}^{-}$ contains the negative real numbers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{R}^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}$ contains all integers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}$ contains the positive integers (natural numbers). Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{N}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}$ contains all real numbers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ belongs to $\\mathbb{R}$.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{Z}$, $\\mathbb{R}$ only.",
