    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a7657785-e632-5b84-9e95-c181a52ea941",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the rational numbers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each set contains all the rational numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}$ contains all rational numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative rational numbers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the rational numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ contains the nonpositive real numbers. For instance, $1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the rational numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}$ contains all real numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{R}$.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{Q}$, $\\mathbb{R}$ only.",
